        <section class="trust-questions" id="questions">
            <div class="activity-wrap trust-questions-grid">
                <header>
                    <span class="activity-eyebrow">Understanding the Trust</span>
                    <h2>Questions families and well-wishers often ask</h2>
                    <p>Clear answers are part of responsible service. These principles explain both the Trust’s focus and the way it protects every contribution.</p>
                </header>
                <div class="trust-accordion">
                    <details>
                        <summary>Why did the Trust support students across existing schools?</summary>
                        <p>Working across schools allows assistance to reach far more girls than a single institution could serve. The Trust can respond wherever verified need arises while students remain connected to their own learning environment.</p>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Why is this Trust focused on girls?</summary>
                        <p>It was created in response to the educational exclusion experienced by girls. Support for boys is organised separately through Gyanyogi Shri Nandkishore Sharda Adhyatm Kendra.</p>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>How are administrative expenses managed?</summary>
                        <p>Members voluntarily bear the Trust’s administrative expenditure, allowing contributions received for education to remain directed toward educational support.</p>
                    </details>
                    <details>
                        <summary>Can someone contribute without making a donation?</summary>
                        <p>Yes. Time, mentorship, professional guidance and sincere voluntary service can all strengthen the circle around students.</p>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

